    2. Create template panel (NxN) with marker pixels forming a pattern of 3 to n*n-2 cells on bg.
    3. Create source panel (NxN) with 2 to n*n-1 non-bg pixels, each colored from the chosen source palette. Ensure at least 2 distinct fg colors used.
    4. Randomly decide panel order (source first or second).
    5. Concatenate panels into Nx2N (LR) or 2NxN (TB) input grid.
    6. Verify solver disambiguates correctly (one panel has exactly 1 fg color, the other has >=2, colors disjoint).


